lider-gallery_scrollbar\"><div fs-slider-element=\"scrollbar-drag\" class=\"fs-slider-gallery_scrollbar_drag\"></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class=\"faq-section\"><div class=\"w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container\"><div data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bc3\" class=\"header-faq\"><h2>Custom Deck FAQs</h2><div>Have questions about composite or wood deck installation in Florida? Our licensed deck builders answer the most common questions from Florida homeowners.</div></div><div class=\"wrapper-faq-components\"><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bc7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Which decking materials are best for Florida homes?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">We use composite decking, pressure-treated lumber, and fiberglass-reinforced boards engineered for long-lasting performance in Florida's heat, humidity, and seasonal rain. These materials resist warping, rot, and pest damage — delivering a surface that maintains its appearance and structural integrity across North and South Florida climates.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bcf\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">How long does a composite deck last in Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Composite decking resists fading, rot, and pest damage — with many leading products backed by manufacturer warranties of 25 years or more. This extended warranty protection, combined with the material's low maintenance requirements, makes composite an excellent long-term value for Florida homeowners investing in outdoor living upgrades.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bd7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Do composite decks stay cool underfoot in Florida heat?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Premium composite decking uses heat-reflective pigments and ventilated profiles that reduce surface temperature compared to standard wood or concrete. Travertine pavers offer a naturally cool surface, making them a popular barefoot-friendly option for Florida pool decks and outdoor living areas exposed to direct South Florida sun.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bdf\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Is deck maintenance required after installation?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Composite and travertine deck surfaces require minimal maintenance. No sealing, staining, or sanding is needed. Periodic pressure washing and joint re-sanding for paver decks keep surfaces clean. These low-maintenance materials withstand heat, rain, and UV exposure — ideal for Florida homeowners seeking long-term durability with minimal upkeep.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077be7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Can you match my home’s existing design style?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Yes. Our deck builders fully customize shapes, levels, railing styles, and surface finishes to complement your home's architecture. From straight-line pool decks in travertine or pavers to multi-level composite platforms with built-in lighting, every deck integrates seamlessly with your Florida outdoor living environment.</p></nav></div></div></div><img sizes=\"100vw\" srcset=\"/images/site/design2-p-500.webp 500w, /images/site/design2-p-800.webp 800w, /images/site/design2-p-1080.webp 1080w, /images/site/design2-p-1600.webp 1600w, /images/site/design2.webp 1920w\" alt=\"\" src=\"/images/site/design2.webp\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"design-bg\"></section></div><section class=\"location\"><div class=\"w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container\"><div data-w-id=\"dfdd7317-58e7-27b3-99a6-2c20a5e8a7be\" class=\"header-location\"><h2>Where We Serve</h2><p>Regional Coverage With National Vision</p></div></div><div class=\"cms-country w-dyn-list\"><div role=\"list\" class=\"cms-list-country w-dyn-items\"><div role=\"listitem\" class=\"item-country w-dyn-item\"><img src=\"/images/where-we-serves/custom-pool-builders-south-florida/custom-inground-pool-builders-remodeling-florida.avif\" loading=\"lazy\" alt